We call the type with higher prior \emph{primary} and the other \emph{secondary}.\footnote{When the prior is $\beliefi{1}{0}=\beliefi{2}{0}=0.5$, the selection of the primary/secondary goal becomes arbitrary. Our results on PBNE still hold for each case.}
