In this subsection, we compare two strategies for constructing the set of test functions: the Multi-scale-Global (MG, \cref{alg:MG}) and Single-scale-Local (SL, \cref{alg:SL}) approaches. The comparison is based on the performance of the WENDy framework in terms of both parameter error and runtime. All computations were performed in parallel on the University of Colorado Boulder's Blanca Condo Cluster, with each trial executed on a single core of an Intel Xeon Platinum 8592+ CPU @ 2.90GHz.

