It has been shown that computational power of Game of Life is equivalent to that of a universal Turing machine~\cite{Berlekamp1982}, and thus, the Game of Life dynamics may be undecidable under some conditions~\cite{prokopenko_self-referential_2019}. In other words, it cannot be determined, for all initial configurations of the Game of Life, whether or not they will reach some predefined final (termination) configurations (see \ref{app-CA}).



