  Assume that either $x\in\noending{H}$ or $y\in\noending{H}$.

  Then there exists a unique $G$-causal curve connecting $x$ to $y$.
\end{proposition}
\begin{proof}
    The existence is given by \Cref{P:G-parametrization}.

  We assume $x\in\noending{H}$, the other case being symmetric.
