       %

  \noindent
  {\bf Step 2.} Construction of the dynamical transport plan.

  \noindent
Let $\hat h_{n}: C_{G_{n}}\to C_{G_\infty, \epsilon_{n}}$
denote the post-composition by $h_{n}$,
(i.e.,
$\hat{h}_{n}(\gamma)=h_{n}\circ \gamma$)
  and define
$\eta_{n}:= (\hat h_{n})_{\sharp}\nu_{n}$.
  %
    We claim that the sequence $(\eta_{n})_{n}$ is tight.
    %
    Up to taking a subsequence, we can assume $\epsilon_{n}$ to be
    decreasing, therefore, by hypothesis, $\eta_{n}$ is concentrated on $C_{G_\infty,\epsilon_{m}}$, if $n\geq m$.
    %
    Since $(h_{n})_{\sharp}\mu_{i}^n\weak \mu_{i}^\infty$, then the family $\{(h_{n})_{\sharp}\mu_{i}^n\}_{i=0,1, n\in \N}$ is tight. For every $\delta>0$, let $K_\delta \subset H_\infty$ be a compact set, such that 
    \[
    (e_{i})_{\sharp}\eta_{n}(K_\delta)=(h_{n})_{\sharp}\mu_{i}^n(K)\geq
