\subsection{Numerical noise} \label{sec:3a}

In numerically integrating Eqs.~(\ref{eq:1})-(\ref{eq:3}) using the forward Euler method, we transform the continuous-time dynamics into a discrete map. We view related errors induced by such a transformation as the primary components of numerical noise, which can sometimes force the system into chaotic behavior.
