	There exist $\bar{\tau}, \bar{\bar{\tau}} \in (0,1)$ with $\bar{\bar{\tau}}\leq \bar{\tau}$ such that it is optimal to choose $\alpha^*>0$ if $\tau_2 \in (\bar{\tau},1]$, and it is optimal to choose $\alpha^*=0$ if $\tau_2 \in [0,\bar{\bar{\tau}})$. 
